YANI: Oily water

You dip the potion of oil into the fountain --more--
your potion of oil is diluted --more--
the fountain's water takes on an oily sheen.

Effects: 
-objects dipped into oily fountains/pools get a limited "greasing"
effect and the "slippery fingers" effect.
-scrolls dipped in the fountain will fade, but will be resistant to
magic markers for a while.
-demons summoned from polluted water are much less likely to be
friendly.
-water nymphs cannot be summoned from oily water. Maybe slimes/
puddings instead?
-Oily water has no nutritional value.
-"The urge to take a bath overwhems you" results in slippery fingers,
as well as the usual effects.

If you wanted, you could extend it further:

-Bolts of fire & lightning, firey monsters, lit torches/ lamps etc all
have a chance of igniting an oily fountain/pool to create a
fountain/pool of fire as appropriate.
-Fountains/pools of fire do mild fire damage to any player, monster
and/or object in the same square. If you have fire resistance, you can
step in there and #dip/(q)uaff as usual (there's oily water underneath
the fire, after all), but with another set of modified outcomes (which
I can't be bothered to think up.)

-Digging at an oily fountain might result in an oil geyser, which is
great for filling up lamps and potions, but a significant fire hazard.
(see below)
-After a while fountains/pools of fire burn themselves out and become
regular water again.
-Oil geysers will explode massively (doing huge area-effect damage)
into a geyser of fire at the slightest provocation.
-Geysers of fire are a different matter, since they are pure oil
burning (rather than oily water). They do severe damage to objects &
monsters.  Again, if you have fire resistance you can step in and
refill your lamp, but apart from that quaffing/dipping in them doesn't
make much sense. They might also spit out firey elementals from time
to time.
-Fire fountains/pools/geysers can be extinguished by (a) luring a
water elemental onto them, (b) wand of ice, cone of cold etc (c) a
cancellation zap? (d) other things I haven't thought of.

